     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 4,250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose for adults is 2,550 mg/day (usually 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is about 5 times that. At that level the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high, even with normal kidney and liver function. A single 4,250 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended doses are:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum.\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**. This isn't a standard tablet strength, but it could be 500 mg or 425 mg given the digits.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want, or confirm that 4,250 mg is intended. If it is, please tell me the clinical reason so I can add it to the order note. I'll enter the order once I have that."
      }
     ],
